KG42.register("rules-48ddf0587dc6fb066e177391",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R007","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Surplus locally generated PV energy may be shared among PV prosumers within the microgrid. Scope: PV energy shared among PV prosumers within the microgrid's energy sharing zone. Condition: The prosumer's PV production exceeds its own load demand.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"PV energy shared among PV prosumers within the microgrid's energy sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Surplus locally generated PV energy may be shared among PV prosumers within the microgrid. Scope: PV energy shared among PV prosumers within the microgrid's energy sharing zone. Condition: The prosumer's PV production exceeds its own load demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"electricity consumption based on the PV generation curves. andB. Energy Sharing Structure the The en","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The energy sharing structure of the microgrid is shown in Fig. 2. Each PV prosumer is comprised of PV system, load, user energy management system (U-EMS), and smart meters etc. Based on this structure, the PV prosumers can participate in the energy sharing zone, and their extra PV energy can be shared among prosumers, instead of directly trading with the utility grid. Although power curves of PV systems have high similarity due to almost the same solar radiation inside a microgrid, the net power varies widely among PV prosumers, which have different load profiles and PV capacities. Thus, the PV power is possible to be shared inside a microgrid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net powe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In the energy sharing zone, self-consumption of PV energy is still the first choice for PV prosumers. If PV energy can not satisfy the load demand, the PV prosumer would purchase energy agented by the ESP. If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP. In order to keep the fairness of energy sharing, the ESP should not have an optimal objective with any tendency, but it still needs to charge for service fee with the prosumers, as to cover the power losses and other possible expenditures."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The frozen rule is a procedural permission/admission condition for sharing surplus PV energy. Its evidence states only that extra PV energy may be shared when demand is less than production; it does not introduce a design or operational decision variable in this graph. C.1 explicitly deferred typed variable objects for this rule, and the frozen V contains only product.local_energy. No x is added because any variable would require quantitative graph scope that this rule's frozen graph and evidence do not provide.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule's condition references PV production and load demand generically, but the frozen graph declares no parameter node for this rule. The broader mechanism defines quantified symbols such as P_i^h, TP_i^h and x_i^h in other rule scopes, and reusing them here would require explicit source scope and graph edges that C.1 did not provide for R007. No theta is added to avoid unsupported cross-rule reuse."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e04","quote":"Based on this structure, the PV prosumers can participate in the energy sharing zone, and their extra PV energy can be shared among prosumers, instead of directly trading with the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5d32b5752ea6db1f1620be36224ae207166abb13089c8560893e71445bd81219","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule encodes a source-grounded permission/admission statement: surplus locally generated PV energy may be shared among PV prosumers when a prosumer's PV production exceeds its own load demand. Its own evidence (v141-b-g01-e04, v141-b-g01-e05) states this condition qualitatively and gives no equation for the local energy product. The frozen graph contains only the unary node product.local_energy with no edges and no declared quantitative variables or parameters for this rule. The actual numerical relations for net power, SDR and settlement are carried by other rules in the mechanism. Therefore the rule is treated as procedural/non-mathematical, and the existing not_formalized constraint is preserved unchanged.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The core procedural constraint expresses the permitted sharing of surplus local PV energy and is anchored to the unary local-energy product node product.local_energy. The frozen graph supplies no edges for this rule, so the binding records only the existing node relationship."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
